# RegAnchor aesthetic (mandatory)

Full reference: [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md). Naming/legal: [BRAND.md](BRAND.md). Tokens: `css/reganchor.css`, `css/portal.css`.

## Before changing UI

1. Open `portal.html` / `css/portal.css` and match that language.
2. Open `index.html` for public marketing chrome and **button pair** behaviour.
3. Do not invent a second theme (especially dark fintech or purple-gradient startup).

## Non-negotiables

- Light paper canvas, ink `#0A0E14`, hairlines `#E6EBF1`, Blurple `#533AFD` **only** for primary actions and score meters
- Inter body; IBM Plex Sans for wordmark and score numerals
- Sentence case chrome — no stamped all-caps
- Severity = typographic colour on the label, never a parent `color` that paints the whole block
- 4px controls; ledgers over decorative cards; no glow/glass/pill clusters
- Product copy = **RegAnchor**; certificates/legal issuer = **MLA Group Ltd**
- PDF templates (`report-template.html`, `certificate-template.html`) stay self-contained CSS for Puppeteer

## Buttons (index is the source of truth — never invent a third pair)

Match `index.html` `.btn-primary` / `.btn-ghost` exactly on every new public surface.

| Control | Rest | Hover / focus |
|---------|------|----------------|
| **Primary** | Blurple fill + white label | Blurple-hover `#4434E0`, still white label |
| **Ghost** (white / outline) | White (or paper) fill, ink label, hairline border | **Blurple border + Blurple label** on quiet paper hover — **not** ink/dark fill |
| **Menus / major actions** | Ink label; muted grey if disabled | Quiet grey wash **plus Blurple label** (same as ghost / wordmark). Keep the grey shader — do not fill the row Blurple. Disabled stays grey, no accent. |

```css
/* Ghost: never darken the fill on hover */
.btn-ghost:hover,
.btn-ghost:focus-visible {
  border-color: var(--accent); /* blurple */
  background: var(--hover);    /* quiet paper hover only */
  color: var(--accent);        /* blurple text — not dark ink */
}

/* Menus / major actions: grey wash stays, label goes Blurple */
.reg-bulk-menu button:hover,
.reg-bulk-menu button:focus-visible {
  background: var(--ra-hover);
  color: var(--ra-blurple);
}
```

Reject: ghost hover that turns black/navy/ink solid, grey-only hover with no Blurple on an enabled major action, primary that greys out on hover.

## Reject these patterns

```html
<!-- BAD: risk colour cascades into every child -->
<div class="dom-band" style="color:${sc.c}">...</div>

<!-- BAD: full-width pink number bar -->
<div class="act-n" style="background:${ph.color}22;color:${ph.color}">1</div>
```

```html
<!-- GOOD: ink hierarchy + meter; risk only on status word -->
<div class="dom-band">
  <div class="dom-concept-name">…</div>
  <div class="dom-meter"><span style="width:39%"></span></div>
  <span class="dom-status-pill is-risk">High risk</span>
</div>
```

If layout CSS for JS-emitted classes is missing, restore layout — do not only swap CSS variables.
